// The complete list of functions whose returned error this repository does not
// require to be handled. It is complete because the gate runs errcheck with
// -excludeonly, so the tool's own built-in list is off and this file is the
// whole rule set. Without that flag, a tool upgrade changes what is enforced
// here without a commit in this repository.
//
// One entry per line, with the reason above it. An entry with no reason is an
// exclusion nobody can argue with later.

// Writing to a strings.Builder cannot fail: its Write methods are documented to
// always return a nil error. Writing to the process's own standard error can
// fail, and a program that cannot reach standard error has nowhere left to
// report that it could not.
fmt.Fprint
fmt.Fprintf
fmt.Fprintln
